`properties` array, and the site answered 201.
`crates/fiddle-runtime/tests/live_jira_filing.rs` is that lane, and ADR 079
carries the record.

MEASURED against the loopback stub, and against nothing else. The run path.
`CveMitigate::execute` calls `file_tickets`, which calls `ticket_proposals` and
executes each `FileVerdict` through the same `Executor`, and it does so only when
`[jira.filing]` names a project, an issue type and a ledger issue.
`crates/fiddle-runtime/tests/cve_filing.rs` holds this. `filing_client` in
`crates/fiddle-cli/src/main.rs` reads that table and attaches the client. ADR 080
carries the decisions.

NOT REACHED. No run of a `fiddle` binary has written to a real site. The live
lane builds a `TicketFiling` itself and reads no `fiddle.toml`, so the route from
the document to the effect is measured against the stub alone. The only run path
to `FileVerdict` through the binary is a full CVE sweep, which needs a scanner,
an agent and a GitHub repository, and which opens a pull request.

ARGUED, by reading two programs. The jq program above and `ticket_proposals` in
